NOTES:

I really wanted to kill Demogorgon but it turns out he can only be
summoned by other demon princes or a Summon Nasties spell in Hell.
Since I already killed all the other demon princes, and I wasn't about
to sit around a Lich waitng for the Big D, he sat this game out.  So
many dead elves.. all in vain.

Speaking of sacrifices, next time I play any spell caster I am NOT
going to get crowned.  I couldn't get a single spellbook out of Anhur
the whole game (except for FoD when I got crowned of course)!  Instead
I got junk like Werebane, Dragonbane, and Trollbane.  What I really
wanted was remove curse and jumping.  Jumping would've been great on
Astral since it is no teleport.

This game I finally FINALLY ecountered a hostile, randomly-generated
Archon!  In all my years of playing I only encounter these when I
wished for one as a pet.  Now I got one of my very own to play with!
Yay!  I tamed him on the fifth casting but he still managed to die very
quickly for some unknown reason.  I kept Demonbane in his memory.

This time around I also took my time and cleared out the Astral plane.
Usually I make a bee line for my altar and ascend, but with the ability
to cast finger of death the astral plane was pretty easy.  Famine and
Pestilence were no problem.  Neither were the priests, high priests,
adventurers, or anything really.  Death was annoying, but nothing 2
magic missiles couldn't take care of.

I managed to finally get gloves of dexterity in the Astral off of a
Valk adventurer.  I'd spent many many turns polypiling just so could
get those, but with no results.  I had been wearing +1 leather gloves,
but these +4's were much nicer!  For desert I got a +7 rustproof Vorpal
Sword from the tourist.  It was really nice of him to flee in fear
instead of cutting my head off!

I also made an important discovery about my high priest ... she is
really easy to kill so be careful where I cast that finger of death!  I
lost my protection for that (and probably angered Anhur) which left me
at -35 A.  I figured a high priest would be harder to kill than
that....

"But Joeb," you say, "your  character dump says -23!"  Well, that is
right.  I couldn't resist offering a fake amulet to the wrong god just
to see the results.  Well, the result was a disintegrated blessed +4
fireproof cloak of magic resistance & blessed +5 fireproof small
shield.  Luckily I retained Magicbane and the Eye, otherwise Death
probably would have killed me on the way back to my altar.

I also learned that Dragons make terrible pets!  They are always eating
which means not fighting!  But my Archon made up for both of them!  Too
bad he doesn't attack riders.  I still had to deal with those on my
own.

Finally, I also learned the value of confused create monster scrolls.
Acid blobs make great rider blockers.

Joeb, chaotic male elven Wizard


